He moved his finger! But how?

23
00:03:01,480 --> 00:03:02,520
What's going on?

24
00:03:02,860 --> 00:03:05,566
He shouldn't be able to
think, let alone move!

25
00:03:07,220 --> 00:03:09,180
Wait, there's no way.

26
00:03:10,400 --> 00:03:15,397
Is his power the same as...

27
00:03:15,480 --> 00:03:16,660
the world's?

28
00:03:19,120 --> 00:03:22,620
Your stand has a lot in
common with my Star Platinum.

29
00:03:23,040 --> 00:03:27,280
Did he mean the world and Star
Platinum are the same type of stand?

30
00:03:32,540 --> 00:03:33,420
Damn it.

31
00:03:34,900 --> 00:03:36,371
Can you see me right now?

32
00:03:36,460 --> 00:03:39,872
Are you consciously moving or
is it an involuntary twitch?

33
00:03:41,680 --> 00:03:43,220
Okay, time's up.

34
00:03:51,640 --> 00:03:53,400
Jotaro, could you see me?

35
00:03:56,740 --> 00:03:57,820
Must I repeat?

36
00:03:57,980 --> 00:04:00,392
I asked if you could follow my movements!

37
00:04:00,660 --> 00:04:01,560
See what?

38
00:04:01,820 --> 00:04:03,232
You're not making sense.

39
00:04:03,340 --> 00:04:05,458
Need to have your eyes checked, Dio.

40
00:04:13,820 --> 00:04:18,137
just you wait you can't run forever
seeing me isn't going to do you any

41
00:04:18,220 --> 00:04:23,957
good when time is standing still if
your stand does bear similarities

42
00:04:24,040 --> 00:04:29,597
to mine prove it i want to see
just how much we have in common yes

43
00:04:29,680 --> 00:04:34,280
it's been six months since i began
to grasp the art of stopping time

44
00:04:38,640 --> 00:04:41,180
To test the world's speed and power,

45
00:04:41,500 --> 00:04:46,000
I commanded my servant to take
aim, point-blank, right at my back.

46
00:04:46,420 --> 00:04:50,820
And for a moment, it looked as
though time itself had stood still.

47
00:04:51,320 --> 00:04:53,780
I thought for sure I was hallucinating.

48
00:04:54,100 --> 00:04:59,037
It seemed like the vision a boxer has when
his opponent's punches linger in mid-air.

49
00:04:59,120 --> 00:05:01,400
That second felt like an eternity.

50
00:05:02,160 --> 00:05:04,580
But I wasn't simply imagining things.

51
00:05:04,960 --> 00:05:07,577
My stand was actually
able to move between the

52
00:05:07,660 --> 00:05:10,307
hovering bullets that
were suspended in time.

53
00:05:12,840 --> 00:05:14,600
And it could grasp them.

54
00:05:18,700 --> 00:05:20,000
Yes, Lord Dio.

55
00:05:20,160 --> 00:05:22,977
You are well on your way to
being the master of time.

56
00:05:23,060 --> 00:05:27,472
The next step is willing yourself to
move through the realm of frozen time.

57
00:05:27,940 --> 00:05:30,037
It must happen as naturally as breathing,

58
00:05:30,120 --> 00:05:34,120
or as nonchalantly as snapping a
pencil betwixt your mighty fingers.

59
00:05:34,400 --> 00:05:36,988
You must think of it
as completely ordinary.

60
00:05:37,200 --> 00:05:40,217
The most important thing is
having faith in yourself.

61
00:05:40,300 --> 00:05:44,418
It's imperative that you find the
mental fortitude to steal your mind.

62
00:05:45,720 --> 00:05:48,440
You are the one true ruler of this world.

63
00:05:48,880 --> 00:05:51,704
Controlling time should
be second nature to you.

64
00:05:54,480 --> 00:06:00,100
Then one day, I sensed the wheels of time
and the world interlock at long last.

65
00:06:00,340 --> 00:06:05,800
Like a ray of clarity dispersing the
shadows in my mind, a revelation befell me.

66
00:06:06,060 --> 00:06:11,980
I was Dio, and my destiny was to surpass
all living things, including stand users!

67
00:06:12,360 --> 00:06:17,066
I can stop time for five seconds, and the
time limit keeps extending by the day!

68
00:06:17,180 --> 00:06:21,120
Now, Jotaro, you're about to
experience just how weak you are!

69
00:06:21,640 --> 00:06:23,522
Time to make good on my promise!

70
00:06:24,320 --> 00:06:27,760
The world grinds to a halt!

71
00:06:58,120 --> 00:07:00,000
I see you planted a magnet.

72
00:07:01,080 --> 00:07:03,717
Must have been when we
were exchanging blows.

73
00:07:03,800 --> 00:07:07,682
It looks like a wallet magnet or
one picked from a pocket planner.

74
00:07:09,280 --> 00:07:11,680
I have to admit, you had me fooled.

75
00:07:11,980 --> 00:07:13,580
You're a clever boy indeed.

76
00:07:14,400 --> 00:07:15,230
But!

77
00:07:16,160 --> 00:07:18,617
If you have to resort to
inane tricks like that,

78
00:07:18,700 --> 00:07:22,237
it only proves that you can't
move while time is standing still.

79
00:07:22,320 --> 00:07:25,437
You've only postponed the
inevitable by a few seconds.

80
00:07:25,520 --> 00:07:26,540
This is the end!

81
00:07:26,860 --> 00:07:28,120
Die, Jotaro!

82
00:07:39,560 --> 00:07:40,390
What?

83
00:07:43,120 --> 00:07:44,560
Oh, no.

84
00:07:45,180 --> 00:07:46,010
He's moving.

85
00:07:46,360 --> 00:07:47,417
What nerve.

86
00:07:47,500 --> 00:07:49,780
Although, he can only do it briefly.

87
00:07:50,340 --> 00:07:53,377
The magnet wasn't meant to
make me think he could move.

88
00:07:53,460 --> 00:07:55,517
It was made to make me think he couldn't.

89
00:07:55,600 --> 00:07:58,360
Damn it, it was a trap
designed to lure me in.

90
00:07:58,660 --> 00:08:00,157
And I fell for it.

91
00:08:00,240 --> 00:08:03,769
The key is believing that your
power is completely ordinary.

92
00:08:04,360 --> 00:08:05,190
Disgusting.

93
00:08:05,280 --> 00:08:10,160
To think that my domain could be invaded,
and by one of the Joestars, no less.

94
00:08:11,140 --> 00:08:12,140
It's infuriating.

95
00:08:24,040 --> 00:08:28,897
I was able to move for a second
there that's a good sign even so

96
00:08:28,980 --> 00:08:33,980
that's not much it would only give
me enough time for a single punch

97
00:08:43,800 --> 00:08:45,280
You there, woman.

98
00:08:46,580 --> 00:08:49,980
How about you make yourself
useful and fetch me my leg?

99
00:08:51,760 --> 00:08:53,348
Bring it here this instant!

100
00:08:53,540 --> 00:08:55,817
Imagine you're a flight
attendant bringing caviar to

101
00:08:55,900 --> 00:08:59,076
a passenger in first class
if it gets you here faster!

102
00:09:06,300 --> 00:09:09,137
well that's good to
know seems i'll have to

103
00:09:09,220 --> 00:09:11,985
blow your head off to do
any significant damage

104
00:09:13,220 --> 00:09:17,102
bastard you've already siphoned
off enough energy to heal yourself

105
00:09:18,400 --> 00:09:22,400
it's like that gaping hole i opened
in your gut was never even there

106
00:09:26,340 --> 00:09:30,217
your eyes followed me even
while time was frozen which

107
00:09:30,300 --> 00:09:33,337
confirms that you can see my
movements Isn't that right,

108
00:09:33,420 --> 00:09:34,250
Jotaro?

109
00:09:36,560 --> 00:09:39,020
Nervous yet, sweetheart? Not at all.

110
00:09:39,440 --> 00:09:41,322
Kakyoin did you quite the favor.

111
00:09:41,460 --> 00:09:45,777
Because of his brilliant mind, he was able
to correctly deduce the world's secret.

112
00:09:45,860 --> 00:09:47,997
And because he passed
that knowledge along,

113
00:09:48,080 --> 00:09:50,037
you figured out that I
could stop time at will

114
00:09:50,120 --> 00:09:53,120
and worked until you learned
how to do it yourself.

115
00:09:53,980 --> 00:09:54,810
Then again,

116
00:09:55,020 --> 00:09:57,137
you haven't had as much
training as I have,

117
00:09:57,220 --> 00:10:01,573
so I'm curious to know exactly how
long you can move while time is frozen.

118
00:10:02,020 --> 00:10:03,740
Two seconds? Or maybe three?

119
00:10:04,140 --> 00:10:06,737
Or perhaps you can move
five seconds like me,

120
00:10:06,820 --> 00:10:10,157
but you're pretending you can't
to gain some kind of an advantage.

121
00:10:10,240 --> 00:10:11,070
Clever.

122
00:10:13,720 --> 00:10:14,880
Which is it?

123
00:10:15,680 --> 00:10:16,780
This isn't good.

124
00:10:17,340 --> 00:10:21,157
I could probably move longer if I
was able to get some practice in.

125
00:10:21,240 --> 00:10:24,580
But as it stands, the
best I can do is a second.

126
00:10:25,380 --> 00:10:30,357
If I was forced to make a guess, I'd
say you could only move for a second.

127
00:10:30,440 --> 00:10:35,100
Be that as it may, you've still
managed to infiltrate my world.

128
00:10:35,480 --> 00:10:37,837
Only a fool would risk
approaching you now,

129
00:10:37,920 --> 00:10:41,597
and though I'm many things, a fool
wouldn't be considered one of them.

130
00:10:41,680 --> 00:10:45,739
While it's achingly clear that my
advantage over you is overwhelming,

131
00:10:46,440 --> 00:10:48,900
I've still devised a way to execute you,

132
00:10:49,080 --> 00:10:54,021
so regardless of how long you can move in
my world, you'll never escape your demise!

133
00:10:54,520 --> 00:10:56,020
You're white as a sheet.

134
00:10:56,220 --> 00:10:57,497
Do these bring back memories?

135
00:10:57,580 --> 00:10:59,817
Do they remind you that
you're going to die a death

136
00:10:59,900 --> 00:11:02,841
even more horrific than
your pathetic grandfather?

137
00:11:03,220 --> 00:11:04,500
Screw this bastard.

138
00:11:04,840 --> 00:11:06,937
How the hell does he come
up with this kind of shit?

139
00:11:07,020 --> 00:11:08,255
I need to be careful.

140
00:11:11,640 --> 00:11:13,020
There is no escape.

141
00:11:14,100 --> 00:11:15,020
The world!

142
00:11:22,600 --> 00:11:23,860
Five seconds left.

143
00:11:28,640 --> 00:11:33,346
Do you think your star platinum can deflect
all of the knives once time resumes?

144
00:11:33,660 --> 00:11:38,425
If I were a betting man, I'd give that
plan a one in a million chance of working.

145
00:11:38,640 --> 00:11:39,660
Four seconds!

146
00:11:42,540 --> 00:11:46,977
It must be terrifying to stare death
in the face and be helpless to stop it!

147
00:11:47,060 --> 00:11:48,820
Only three seconds remain!

148
00:11:57,140 --> 00:11:59,857
you're down to two seconds are you telling

149
00:11:59,940 --> 00:12:03,697
me that's the best you've
got that's just more

150
00:12:03,780 --> 00:12:05,897
evidence of your ineptitude
in the presence of

151
00:12:05,980 --> 00:12:12,760
one such as myself one
second left to go zero

152
00:12:26,980 --> 00:12:27,940
It's over.

153
00:12:28,340 --> 00:12:30,340
But one can never be too careful.

154
00:12:36,220 --> 00:12:38,040
Now, to be perfectly honest,

155
00:12:38,360 --> 00:12:42,125
I'm relieved I was able to do
away with you so quickly, Chotaro.

156
00:12:43,480 --> 00:12:44,657
I have to say,

157
00:12:44,740 --> 00:12:49,681
I never would have thought that you'd have
the power to infiltrate my perfect world.

158
00:12:49,960 --> 00:12:51,180
Now, let's see.

159
00:12:51,600 --> 00:12:54,071
A fitting analogy would be the automobile.

160
00:12:54,520 --> 00:12:58,108
Useful machines until the roads
become clogged with them all.

161
00:13:00,460 --> 00:13:04,920
Sorry, but the mantle of Master
of Time is reserved for me alone.

162
00:13:20,640 --> 00:13:22,077
Oh, good grief.

163
00:13:22,160 --> 00:13:23,837
He'd throw enough knives or what?

164
00:13:23,920 --> 00:13:27,214
I mean, he'd turn my favorite
uniform into Swiss cheese.

165
00:13:29,420 --> 00:13:32,949
Well, I'm glad I decided to
stuff my clothes with magazines.

166
00:13:33,340 --> 00:13:36,797
I figured it was only a matter of
time before he tried throwing weapons,

167
00:13:36,880 --> 00:13:39,260
but I didn't expect that many.

168
00:13:40,240 --> 00:13:43,577
My best bet right now
is to play possum and

169
00:13:43,660 --> 00:13:46,131
wait for a chance to take Dio by surprise.

170
00:13:46,740 --> 00:13:51,446
Since he can regenerate, I've got to bash
his brains in or else he'll never die.

171
00:13:59,280 --> 00:14:02,221
I believe I'll do one more
check for good measure.

172
00:14:02,680 --> 00:14:05,397
The Joestars have a way of
coming back from the dead.

173
00:14:05,480 --> 00:14:08,833
And there's a chance Jotaro
is putting on this death act.

174
00:14:10,440 --> 00:14:12,460
I need to make sure he's gone.

175
00:14:12,860 --> 00:14:13,820
For good.

176
00:14:15,960 --> 00:14:21,820
I'll use this to sever that
troublesome head of his!

177
00:14:28,000 --> 00:14:29,940
It's time for you to die!

178
00:14:32,040 --> 00:14:33,100
Shotaro! No!

179
00:14:44,980 --> 00:14:47,360
The only one dying here is you!

180
00:14:54,740 --> 00:14:57,360
You're the one who's gonna die! Polnareff!

181
00:15:04,620 --> 00:15:06,020
Time has stopped.

182
00:15:06,320 --> 00:15:08,379
Let's get a good look at your face.

183
00:15:11,660 --> 00:15:12,680
I see.

184
00:15:13,000 --> 00:15:14,140
It's Polnareff.

185
00:15:16,120 --> 00:15:18,000
And now time will resume.

186
00:15:22,560 --> 00:15:24,460
What a shame, Polnareff.

187
00:15:24,580 --> 00:15:26,933
You were so close, but dropped the ball.

188
00:15:27,140 --> 00:15:29,797
If you'd lunged with more
force behind your attack,

189
00:15:29,880 --> 00:15:33,939
You could have eviscerated my brain
beyond the point of regeneration.

190
00:15:35,400 --> 00:15:36,520
You bastard.

191
00:15:37,020 --> 00:15:38,660
It's not over yet.

192
00:15:39,820 --> 00:15:42,760
When will you all accept
that you cannot kill me?

193
00:15:43,080 --> 00:15:46,609
You are nothing more than pawns
destined to be put in check.

194
00:15:47,020 --> 00:15:51,340
Your death brings about the end of
the Joestar's tragic Egyptian journey.

195
00:15:51,880 --> 00:15:52,710
Damn it.

196
00:15:52,793 --> 00:15:55,818
If I don't do something,
Polnareff's as good as dead.

197
00:15:57,500 --> 00:15:59,497
I was going to keep up
this act until I had a

198
00:15:59,580 --> 00:16:02,521
chance to catch him off
guard and crush his skull.

199
00:16:02,820 --> 00:16:07,055
But saving Polnareff from this United
freak is more important right now.

200
00:16:07,800 --> 00:16:09,137
It's not going to be easy, though.

201
00:16:09,220 --> 00:16:12,957
He won't make the mistake of
crossing into Star Platinum's range,

202
00:16:13,040 --> 00:16:15,897
so it'll just end up like
the last time he trapped me.

203
00:16:15,980 --> 00:16:18,686
Whatever I do, I can't
let him know I'm alive.

204
00:16:18,860 --> 00:16:20,517
As long as he thinks I'm dead,

205
00:16:20,600 --> 00:16:22,017
I have the element of surprise,

206
00:16:22,100 --> 00:16:26,237
which gives me a chance to get in
close strange how things end up

207
00:16:26,320 --> 00:16:30,197
coming full circle one minute i'm
trying to will myself to move through

208
00:16:30,280 --> 00:16:33,877
a world of frozen time and the next
i'm doing everything i can to stay

209
00:16:33,960 --> 00:16:37,237
completely still enjoy your journey

210
00:16:37,320 --> 00:16:38,297
to the afterlife

211
00:16:38,380 --> 00:16:45,080
damn you jojaro

212
00:16:48,920 --> 00:16:53,260
was he alive all along at the very
least he seems to be coming too

213
00:16:55,840 --> 00:16:56,670
Hold it!

214
00:16:57,260 --> 00:16:58,520
This is the police!

215
00:16:58,700 --> 00:17:01,017
You try anything funny and we will shoot!

216
00:17:01,100 --> 00:17:03,041
Slowly put your hands in the air!

217
00:17:08,260 --> 00:17:10,420
Ah, what impeccable timing.

218
00:17:11,080 --> 00:17:14,497
If you wouldn't mind, there's
somebody I'd like for you to shoot.

219
00:17:14,580 --> 00:17:16,933
Do you see that man lying on the ground?

220
00:17:17,120 --> 00:17:19,020
Shoot his leg or torso.

221
00:17:21,600 --> 00:17:22,430
That's right.

222
00:17:22,513 --> 00:17:25,342
Alright, line up the shot
and let the bullet fly.

223
00:17:32,680 --> 00:17:35,760
I thought I heard Jotaro
make a sound a moment ago,

224
00:17:35,900 --> 00:17:38,547
but I guess my mind was
playing tricks on me.

225
00:17:44,120 --> 00:17:46,000
Could he be any more demented?

226
00:17:46,680 --> 00:17:48,917
He's at least lost interest in Polnareff.

227
00:17:49,000 --> 00:17:52,960
But now that his attention's back
on me, he's even more suspicious.

228
00:17:53,560 --> 00:17:56,207
He's not gonna rest
until he's sure I'm dead.

229
00:17:56,700 --> 00:17:58,406
Things just got a lot harder.

230
00:17:58,720 --> 00:17:59,550
I know.

231
00:17:59,660 --> 00:18:01,601
Why don't we check his breathing?

232
00:18:05,100 --> 00:18:06,080
No luck.

233
00:18:06,460 --> 00:18:07,760
He's not breathing.

234
00:18:08,740 --> 00:18:11,400
But there's no way to hide his heartbeat.

235
00:18:26,860 --> 00:18:28,040
Shit, this hurts.

236
00:18:28,400 --> 00:18:32,437
If I black out, everything we've been
through will have been for nothing.

237
00:18:32,520 --> 00:18:35,520
Dying because I used my
own stand to stop my heart.

238
00:18:35,920 --> 00:18:37,000
It'd be ironic.

239
00:18:37,400 --> 00:18:38,940
In a morbid kind of way.

240
00:18:43,680 --> 00:18:45,920
And sure enough, there's no heartbeat.

241
00:18:46,300 --> 00:18:47,197
What do you know?

242
00:18:47,280 --> 00:18:51,868
I suppose the thought of him being alive
was just a figment of my imagination.

243
00:18:52,780 --> 00:18:54,956
Though stranger things have happened,

244
00:18:55,120 --> 00:18:58,355
so I should still probably
lop off his head to be sure.

245
00:18:58,720 --> 00:19:00,420
That's not a problem, is it?

246
00:19:13,220 --> 00:19:14,050
What?

247
00:19:20,320 --> 00:19:22,120
I have to stop time again!

248
00:19:22,560 --> 00:19:23,620
The world!

249
00:19:25,580 --> 00:19:27,080
I gotta hand it to you.

250
00:19:27,320 --> 00:19:29,537
You really put me through hell back there.

251
00:19:29,620 --> 00:19:32,417
You're not stopping time or
leaving with your skull intact.

252
00:19:32,500 --> 00:19:33,330
Got it?

253
00:19:34,800 --> 00:19:35,630
No!

254
00:19:35,760 --> 00:19:37,840
This can't be happening to me!

255
00:19:43,940 --> 00:19:45,617
It took long enough.

256
00:19:45,700 --> 00:19:49,660
I finally got to run my fist
straight through his demented skull.

257
00:19:50,440 --> 00:19:55,381
But that walking cesspool of evil lived at
the bottom of the sea for over a century.

258
00:19:55,560 --> 00:19:57,860
I can't be sure that attack killed him.

259
00:19:58,320 --> 00:20:00,849
It's a bit too early
to take a victory lap.

260
00:20:06,480 --> 00:20:08,840
I will annihilate you!

261
00:20:11,220 --> 00:20:12,320
What the hell?

262
00:20:12,760 --> 00:20:14,097
I can't move!

263
00:20:14,180 --> 00:20:16,800
Jotaro, what did you do to me?

264
00:20:17,180 --> 00:20:19,300
I don't have control over my legs!

265
00:20:19,520 --> 00:20:20,860
I can't even stand!

266
00:20:23,520 --> 00:20:24,500
My head!

267
00:20:24,760 --> 00:20:26,380
The pain is unbearable!

268
00:20:27,040 --> 00:20:28,840
I think I'm going to vomit!

269
00:20:29,100 --> 00:20:30,865
This can't be happening to me!

270
00:20:31,040 --> 00:20:32,920
I'm the pinnacle of perfection!

271
00:20:33,680 --> 00:20:37,460
He actually damaged my
brain and paralyzed my legs!

272
00:20:38,180 --> 00:20:39,640
Shit, shit, shit!

273
00:20:39,860 --> 00:20:41,919
I've got to find a way out of here!

274
00:20:45,880 --> 00:20:50,437
I doused you with gasoline so you
can't hide normally I would hate to

275
00:20:50,520 --> 00:20:54,940
kick a guy when he's down on his luck
but with you I don't give a damn.

276
00:20:55,240 --> 00:21:00,340
You killed my friends and countless innocent
bystanders so don't expect any mercy

277
00:21:10,540 --> 00:21:14,140
Come forth, the world!

278
00:21:18,720 --> 00:21:24,560
If I can just make it a little farther.

279
00:21:29,760 --> 00:21:32,540
And now, time will flow as usual!

280
00:21:37,320 --> 00:21:41,908
While he had his ear to the ground, he
was also listening for any nearby cars.

281
00:21:42,260 --> 00:21:43,277
Clever, but...

282
00:21:43,360 --> 00:21:45,654
Bastard's not getting away that easily!

283
00:21:58,640 --> 00:21:59,880
Keep going

284
00:22:00,780 --> 00:22:03,740
That's it I'm almost there

285
00:22:05,480 --> 00:22:07,640
And where do you think you're going?

286
00:22:07,880 --> 00:22:09,586
We've got unfinished business

287
00:22:12,580 --> 00:22:15,560
It's over, Dio Time to accept it!

288
00:22:26,540 --> 00:22:28,480
The world! Free!

289
00:22:44,020 --> 00:22:45,980
You fell for it, Jotaro!

290
00:22:46,300 --> 00:22:48,680
Now my victory is all but assured!

291
00:22:49,060 --> 00:22:52,320
Once again, my genius
has triumphed over you!

292
00:22:52,680 --> 00:22:54,680
Doesn't this street look familiar?

293
00:23:00,860 --> 00:23:02,217
This street...

294
00:23:02,300 --> 00:23:04,400
what have I done?

295
00:23:08,760 --> 00:23:10,200
You failed.

296
00:23:10,620 --> 00:23:13,057
This was my escape route
to your grandfather.

297
00:23:13,140 --> 00:23:15,480
And now his blood is mine!

298
00:23:21,160 --> 00:23:22,097
T .O.

299
00:23:22,180 --> 00:23:23,200
You're dead!

300
00:23:28,160 --> 00:23:31,000
Jotaro, it's been quite
the journey, eh, my boy?

301
00:23:31,180 --> 00:23:34,077
The blood of the Joestars
courses through my veins!

302
00:23:34,160 --> 00:23:37,037
The blood of the Joestars
courses through my veins!

303
00:23:37,120 --> 00:23:41,591
This whole thing might have ended
differently, but you wouldn't piss me off.
